1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,084
In nineteen sixty-nine, Laurence Peter made a joke that

2
00:00:03,942 --> 00:00:07,137
stuck: in any hierarchy, people rise to their level

3
00:00:07,018 --> 00:00:08,124
of incompetence.

4
00:00:08,490 --> 00:00:11,767
Forty years later, three researchers in Italy built that

5
00:00:11,625 --> 00:00:14,704
company inside a computer: a hundred and sixty people,

6
00:00:14,551 --> 00:00:15,679
on six floors.

7
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:18,463
Every year, anyone who is bad at their job

8
00:00:18,321 --> 00:00:21,621
is fired, anyone over sixty retires, and each empty

9
00:00:21,467 --> 00:00:23,630
desk goes to someone from the floor below.

10
00:00:23,926 --> 00:00:26,483
Common sense says: promote the best. If you're good

11
00:00:26,318 --> 00:00:28,038
at your job, you'll be good at the next

12
00:00:27,908 --> 00:00:28,410
one.

13
00:00:28,776 --> 00:00:31,008
But the next job is often a different job.

14
00:00:30,866 --> 00:00:33,968
A great salesperson can make a terrible sales manager.

15
00:00:34,276 --> 00:00:37,193
So the researchers tried a second rule, Peter's rule:

16
00:00:37,086 --> 00:00:40,386
after a promotion, your competence starts over, at random.

17
00:00:40,845 --> 00:00:43,576
Under Peter's rule, promoting the best made the whole

18
00:00:43,411 --> 00:00:46,815
company worse. Its efficiency fell by about ten points.

19
00:00:47,239 --> 00:00:49,668
Good workers kept climbing until they landed in a

20
00:00:49,526 --> 00:00:51,642
job they were bad at. And there they stayed.

21
00:00:52,066 --> 00:00:54,832
Stranger still, promoting the worst made it better, by

22
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:55,866
about twelve points.

23
00:00:56,197 --> 00:00:58,846
Since nobody knows which rule is true, the safest

24
00:00:58,693 --> 00:01:01,052
choice was a coin flip: promote the best or

25
00:01:00,910 --> 00:01:02,213
the worst, at random.

26
00:01:02,498 --> 00:01:04,904
Sometimes the rule that feels fairest is also the

27
00:01:04,762 --> 00:01:05,833
riskiest one.

